From 548117824522bbe8550276c19116d090054f6493 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:52:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] service: Nintendo's NDM module with the online LLE modules

Tangelo's own NDM only stubs SuspendDaemons/ResumeDaemons, so the real
SpotPass module never ran its background schedule: every task that a game
doesn't start itself stayed "not started" (StreetPass relay, notifications,
Golf tournaments, Tomodachi letters, ...), and the friends module didn't
send its presence. With NDM 0004013000002B02 from the NAND they all ran
within a minute (user test 2026-10-15). "Enable required LLE modules for
online features" now loads NDM too, like BOSS, FRD, CECD, NIM and ACT, so
no hand edit of the config is needed. Without the title in the NAND the
HLE NDM stays in use, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
---
 src/core/hle/service/service.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/hle/service/service.cpp b/src/core/hle/service/service.cpp
index ed81a5b4a..e0a7a6b7d 100644
--- a/src/core/hle/service/service.cpp
+++ b/src/core/hle/service/service.cpp
@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@ const std::array<ServiceModuleInfo, 41> service_module_map{
      {"IR", 0x00040130'00003302, IR::InstallInterfaces, false},
      {"MIC", 0x00040130'00002002, MIC::InstallInterfaces, false},
      {"MVD", 0x00040130'20004102, MVD::InstallInterfaces, false},
-     {"NDM", 0x00040130'00002B02, NDM::InstallInterfaces, false},
+     {"NDM", 0x00040130'00002B02, NDM::InstallInterfaces, true},
      {"NEWS", 0x00040130'00003502, NEWS::InstallInterfaces, false},
      {"NFC", 0x00040130'00004002, NFC::InstallInterfaces, false},
      {"NIM", 0x00040130'00002C02, NIM::InstallInterfaces, true},
